{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966792,"nonce":"/aDSg9KQlQL3VnbiAczhGBZKCgg=","title":".foreground() + CSS animation silently breaks composite promotion — fg prims strand outside","message":"A `.foreground()` element that also carries a promotable CSS `@keyframes` (opacity/scale/translateY) gets composite-promoted like any other, but the promotion machinery then silently drops it. This was the cn::select / cn::combobox dropdown fade break: panel bg/border/shadow never appeared while animating, and item text popped to full opacity before the panel faded (\"text before container\" + \"double text\"). cn::menubar was immune because it pushes content through the overlay stack (`is_overlay_root`), not `.foreground()`.\n\n**Why.** During the foreground pass `set_foreground_layer(true)` routes every emit through the `is_foreground` branch → `push_foreground` → `scratch.foreground_primitives`. But the composite region bracket (`bg_primitive_count`), its AABB (`bg_primitive_aabb`), and the subtree bake (`render_subtree_to_layer_texture`) ALL read only `batch.primitives`. So a promoted `.foreground()` panel records an empty region (`end == start`) → no `DynamicKind::CssAnimated` → never baked → never blitted. Its text, collected at BASE alpha under the composite-ancestor contract, then had no live patch because the patch pool is built only over `motion_subtree_texts` and `is_foreground` is checked BEFORE `in_motion_subtree` in the collect partition.\n\n**Fix (blinc_gpu/src/paint.rs + blinc_app/src/context.rs).**\n1. `emit_foreground()` = `is_foreground \u0026\u0026 active_composite_layer.is_none()`. All 14 emit gates use it instead of raw `self.is_foreground`. Inside a composite layer the fg/bg split is meaningless (the whole scratch bakes to one texture blitted as a unit), so foreground emits collapse into `.primitives` and the existing single-list bracket + bake work unchanged.\n2. Collect partition: elements with `composite_ancestor.is_some()` route to the motion pool BEFORE the `is_foreground` (text) / default (svg) arm, so they land in the live-patched `motion_subtree_texts` / `motion_subtree_svgs`.\n\nBoth gated so normal foreground content and non-promoted paths are untouched. Part of gotcha overlay css fade completes without input. The alternative considered and rejected (per user) was migrating select/combobox back onto the overlay stack like menubar — feasible (the original migrate-away reason, unreliable click delivery, is resolved, and focused-input-in-overlay is precedented) but a larger refactor; the compositor fix is surgical and fixes the general `.foreground()`+animation class.","files":null}]}